    "guide_mode": "instructions",
    "guide_steps": [
      {
        "text": "**Make a dog with three moods.** Make a dog image and name it **happy**. Then make **sad** and **confused** - in the new-image dialog, choose *happy* under **Start from** so it stays the same dog, and say what changes, like \"the same dog, looking sad\". Then make **food**, a **bone** and a **toy**."
      },
      {
        "text": "**Now let the model decide.** Head to the **Code** tab.",
        "after": {
          "images": 11
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "**Set the scene, then ask the model.** Add a background and make your dog. Make the food, bone and toy with **make new sprite at ... with behavior being draggable**, so you can move them. Then add **when a sprite is dropped**, and inside it **set [dog] image to (predict with dogmood4)** - each slot is the distance from your dog to one thing. Press **Play** and drag things toward the dog.",
        "after": {
          "tab": "Code"
        }
      }
    ],
    "long_instructions": "# Ask the model\nMake a dog and some things to bring near it. Each time you drop something, the model decides how the dog feels from how close everything is.",
    "toolbox_definition": {
      "kind": "flyoutToolbox",
      "contents": [
        {
          "kind": "block",
          "type": "gamelab_setBackgroundImageAs"
        },
        {
          "kind": "block",
